      "result_text": "I tightened the intro paragraph of `/brief.md` and saved it as version 3. The rest of the brief is unchanged.\n\n**New intro:**\n\n> Tandem is a shared workspace where a team keeps its canonical files and project context in one place, and where each teammate can use their own AI assistant to read and update those files through a remote MCP server. Read this brief before any other document: it explains what we are building, why, and what is out of scope for the Cal Hacks 13.0 demo.\n\n**What I changed:**\n- I cut filler such as \"its project context\", \"keep using\", \"the version that we are going to demo\", and the repeated \"because it explains\".\n- I split the long second sentence into a short instruction plus a short list of what the brief covers.\n- I kept the meaning the same.\n\nI read `/brief.md` at version 2 and saved version 3.",
